=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/SchemaDrift (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/SchemaDrift   kind=page   web route=/admin/schema-drift
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/SchemaDriftPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage do. The generated prompt's idealized "SchemaDriftPage.xaml +
  SchemaDriftPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface
  registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("SchemaDrift", already in RouteTable.cs →
  /admin/schema-drift).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useSchemaDrift (GET /admin/observability/schema-drift). The
  view-model reads through an injected ISchemaDriftFeed; the default EmptySchemaDriftFeed resolves the empty state
  (matching the ApiLogsPage/FeedbackQueuePage host-injection precedent), and the generated-client-backed
  SchemaDriftClientFeed (SchemaDriftPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI contract client operation
  get_api_v1_admin_observability_schema_drift (no params), asserted in tests via the FakeApiClient. No HTTP touches
  the view. A non-success response surfaces as ApiException; the view-model maps StatusCode==503 to the distinct
  subsystem-unavailable banner (web `subsystemMissing`) and every other failure to the generic InfoBar+Retry.
- The web page renders all four data states INSIDE the PageContainer body (PageContainer is passed only `query=` for
  the freshness chip, not loading/error/empty), so the native port reproduces them as visible Fluent regions per
  ADR-006: loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton(3) shimmer; error -> TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry;
  503 subsystem-missing -> TsAlertBanner(Warning) notConfigured; empty -> TsGlassPanel + TsEmptyState; success ->
  the drift-summary + fingerprints glass panels. Never a blank region.
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing fields on this admin surface — SHA fingerprints + table/column/index counts only);
  counts format through the shared NumberFormatting port (web fmtNumber) and the seed timestamp through
  DateTimeFormatting (web formatDateTime) at the display boundary.
- All 22 i18n keys were added verbatim (web key names) to Strings/en/Resources.resw as translation.admin.schemaDrift.*
  (21) + translation.admin.subsystem.unavailableTitle (1), alphabetically placed; the surface resolves them through
  the ILocalizer facade. The ar/he catalogs already lag en by design (translations land later); the app falls back
  to the English default via ILocalizer until translated.
- Pre-existing blocker repaired: TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj had been re-corrupted by its documented .gitattributes
  merge=union strategy into THREE <Project> roots (MSB4025: multiple root elements at line 1380), which failed XML
  load and blocked the whole-solution build at baseline. Regenerated it into the single canonical Project root the
  file's own INVARIANT mandates: the case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted, Include-deduplicated union of every
  Microsoft.UI-free .cs on disk under dashboard-widgets/, feature-views/, misc-surfaces/, modals-dialogs/,
  shared-surfaces/ and widget-primitives/ (doc-comment mentions of Microsoft.UI are not treated as usage). The
  regenerated union reproduced the prior 1327-link set exactly (0 added, 0 dropped) before adding the 3 new
  SchemaDriftPage Model/Source/ViewModel links (1330 total); the bare WinUI view is excluded (it uses Microsoft.UI).

